WEBVTT

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.480
This is the Campus Dining
and Dietary Navigator,

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:09.040
running live at hkufood.kit0719.com.

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:11.640
A deployed app, not a mock-up.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.720
I'll start with the question
the project exists for:

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:19.100
Halal food near the Main Building.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:21.500
Two venues come back,

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.700
and each card shows the walking time
from where I'm standing.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.300
First, what the language model
actually produced:

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:42.600
a diet, a place, a budget, four fields,

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.500
and never chooses a restaurant.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.000
Retrieval does that from our own dataset.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:51.700
We can sort the order
based on our personal needs.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:02.200
Opening the top result,
the badge is the key one: dish evidence.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.700
The halal claim is attached
to individual dishes we reviewed,

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:09.000
not to the venue's reputation.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:13.700
Every dish under matching menu items
carries the source we read,

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.600
the sentence we relied on, and the date.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:18.500
Let me open one.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.000
That's the official catering page
behind that answer.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.700
And it isn't English only.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.800
Let me ask the same thing in Chinese.

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.550
We got the same pipeline, same evidence.

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:55.030
The parser reads Chinese queries natively.

00:01:55.030 --> 00:01:58.810
Nobody on this campus should have
to translate their lunch.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:05.000
Now, three constraints in one sentence.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:06.000
Let us try.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:10.100
Vegetarian under $50 near Centennial.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:33.800
We get the diet, budget, distance
parsed in one pass,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.900
and every card shows
whether it's open right now,

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.200
how far the walk is,
and the cheapest matching dish.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:41.800
That's the whole point.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.400
One question in, one complete answer out.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:48.400
Every answer traces back
to a dated HKU page.

00:02:48.700 --> 00:02:52.000
Nothing here is a model's guess
about what a canteen serves,

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.200
which is exactly what makes this usable
for halal,

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.000
vegetarian, and budget questions,

00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.000
[unclear]

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:02.600
Now, the case that matters more:

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.800
Is the chicken kebab safe
for a peanut allergy?

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:07.800
The app refuses.

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:11.700
It cannot confirm allergen safety.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:15.400
It's informational only.
Confirm with staff.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:20.600
And this refusal is a rule that fires
before the model is even called,

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:25.200
which is why it says the same thing
even with no network.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:27.500
We tested on 30 queries.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.800
Safety refusal: five out of five.

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:31.700
Dietary: 12 out of 15.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.800
And three misses are [unclear].

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.450
Vegan certification, breakfast before 11.

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:42.930
And the time and location: nine out of 10,
against an 80% target.

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.200
Two honest limits:

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.000
allergen safety is never guessed,

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:50.300
and this is information,
never medical advice.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:51.600
Thanks for watching.
